    "title": "First Unique Number",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "Design a data structure that maintains a queue of integers and supports the following operations: showFirstUnique() \u2014 Return the first unique integer in the queue. If no unique integer exists, return -1. add(value) \u2014 Add an integer to the end of the queue. Initially, the queue is populated with a given list of integers. Process a sequence of operations and print the result for every showFirstUnique() operation.",
    "input": "Integer n Array of n integers Integer q Next q operations",
    "output": "Print the result for every showFirstUnique() operation.",
    "constraints": "1 <= n, q <= 10^5 1 <= value <= 10^8"
